ould have a link to D? Let's think. Suppose there's a chain that connects H to D via Indigo 10. But the existing links are from I to A to B to C to D. H isn't part of that chain. Unless there's a rule that connects H to this chain. But the records don't mention H having any Amber or Indigo links directly. \n\nSo, unless there's a rule that somehow connects H to another job in the chain, we can't infer that H has an Indigo 10 link to D. Therefore, the antecedent of Record 12 (H has Indigo 10 to D) is unknown. If we can't confirm that H has that link, then the implication in Record 12 doesn't apply. \n\nSince Record 12's condition isn't met (we don't know if H has Indigo 10 to D), we can't conclude that H doesn't have Ochre 9. Also, there's no direct information about H having Ochre 9. The only status we know for H is Jade 3. \n\nTherefore, the status Ochre 9 for H is neither supported nor contradicted by the given records. The answer should be undetermined.\n</think>\n\n{\"answer\": \"B\"}",
